web-calculator/
│
├── README.md             # Project description and instructions
├── LICENSE               # License file (e.g., MIT)
├── .gitignore            # Ignore unnecessary files
│
├── index.html            # Main HTML file (structure of calculator)
├── style.css             # CSS file (styling and layout)
├── script.js             # JavaScript file (calculator logic)
│
├── assets/               # Optional: images, icons, or sounds
│   └── favicon.png
│
└── display_in_colab.py   # Optional: Python helper to display calculator in Google Colab
🔑 Explanation of Files
index.html → Contains the calculator’s HTML structure.

style.css → Styles the calculator (colors, layout, responsive design).

script.js → Handles calculator logic (number input, operators, clear, equals).

assets/ → Optional folder for icons or images used in the calculator.

display_in_colab.py → Optional Python helper to render the calculator inside Google Colab notebooks.

README.md → Overview, usage instructions, and project description.

LICENSE → License file so others know how they can use your code.
